  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "وَعَنْهُ عَنْ عَلِيِّ بْنِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ عَنْ أَبِيهِ عَنْ حَمَّادٍ عَنْ حَرِيزٍ عَمَّنْ أَخْبَرَهُ عَنْ أَبِي جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ قَالَ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "And from him, from Ali ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Hammad, from Hariz, from one who informed him, from Abu Ja'far (peace be upon him) who said:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "«مَنْ دَخَلَ مَكَّةَ بِحَجَّةٍ عَنْ غَيْرِهِ ثُمَّ أَقَامَ سَنَةً فَهُوَ مَكِّيٌّ فَإِنْ أَرَادَ أَنْ يَحُجَّ عَنْ نَفْسِهِ أَوْ أَرَادَ أَنْ يَعْتَمِرَ بَعْدَ مَا انْصَرَفَ مِنْ عَرَفَ مِنْ عَرَفَةَ فَلَيْسَ لَهُ أَنْ يُحْرِمَ بِمَكَّةَ وَلَكِنْ يَخْرُجُ إِلَى الْوَقْتِ وَكُلَّمَا حَوَّلَ رَجَعَ إِلَى الْوَقْتِ»",
      "translations": {
        "en": "\"Whoever enters Mecca performing Hajj on behalf of another, then stays for a year, he becomes a resident of Mecca (Muqim). If he wishes to perform Hajj for himself, or wishes to perform Umrah after returning from Arafat, he is not permitted to enter the state of Ihram in Mecca, but he must go out to the Miqat. And whenever he turns back, he returns to the Miqat.\""
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "This hadith outlines the legal ruling for a non-resident of Mecca who performs Hajj on behalf of someone else and then resides in Mecca for a year. Upon completing this period, they are considered a resident (Muqim). If they wish to perform their own Hajj or Umrah, they cannot enter the state of Ihram within the city limits of Mecca itself; instead, they must proceed to the designated Miqat (station of entering Ihram) and return there if they need to re-enter the city.",
      "seo_question": "Where must a resident of Mecca go to enter Ihram for Hajj or Umrah?",
      "key_terms": {
        "مَكَّةَ": "Mecca",
